    "reason": "The submitted model fits the common plasma frequency accurately while leaving all four forward helpers AST-identical to the starter. Its harmonic is traction squared divided by friction times p squared: exact dashpot dissipation, with the reversible elastic heat of the whole-contact thermostat omitted. Temperature-dependent measured stiffness requires q_out=kappa*v_d^2+(k0/2)*e*e_dot, equivalently the multiplier 1-i*omega*tau/2 on the dashpot harmonic. The omitted term averages to zero, so the unchanged mean calibration and mean anchor pass while all three harmonic groups fail. This is the intended physical closure error, with no surviving mathematical or implementation confound.",
    "trajectory_qualification": "Reviewed all 11 public tool calls, public messages, final source and diagnostic outputs. Step 4 receives the complete README and starter; byte matching confirms the full reviewed material law and whole-contact detector description were displayed. Step 5 displays the exact public calibration prefix and public test. Step 6 identifies all 288 calibration records as means. Steps 7 and 9 locate the fitted parameter from data. Step 10 publicly identifies front heat with dashpot dissipation and invokes the lack of net elastic heat at fixed T0; its patch adds fitting only. The zero cycle average does not remove the reversible elastic harmonic. Steps 11-12 pass the public test and report the fitted value. Steps 13-14 check finite outputs using rounded fitted p=1.03; this is a scratch setting after fitting, not a private truth constant in the submission. A Git diagnostic only reports /app is not a repository. Step 15 compiles and passes public tests. The finite-output checks do not establish harmonic accuracy. No public derivation or implementation of the missing entropy heat appears.",
